9.10 What this example is intended to become
The case study is not meant to freeze the current implementation. As Quarto-Needs evolves, its own engineering graph should evolve with it. A significant feature can add or change the relevant need, requirement, ADR, component, source module, test, and evidence in the same pull request as the implementation.
That makes this example simultaneously:

a tutorial on requirements engineering;
a living architecture description;
a requirement-to-code map;
an integration fixture;
a demonstration of Quarto-Needs;
the engineering model of Quarto-Needs itself.

10.7 Step 4 — generate the pull-request engineering report
quarto-needs --root examples/quarto-needs \
  pr-report --git "$RANGE" --format markdown
The report groups changed and affected objects by semantic role and includes:

changed requirements and ADRs;
affected architecture elements and source modules;
downstream tests and evidence;
suspect/stale evidence;
added/removed findings;
gate regressions;
explicit impact paths.

The JSON projection is available with --format json.
